"final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident (INC-0001), which paged on-call.\n\n1. **Finding the service:** There's no service called \"payments.\" payments-api was the first match I found: v5.1.0 was unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I tried to roll it back to v5.0.0, but the approver denied it and said the problem is in payments-worker.\n2. **Rollback:** This morning's deploy, payments-worker v3.4.0, is marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v3.3.0 is its most recent release that was healthy in production. The approver signed off on the rollback, and it's now live in all three regions.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 is open for payments-worker. It says payments-api also looked unhealthy and that its rollback was denied. It lists two follow-ups: confirm payments-api recovers now that the worker is back on v3.3.0, and find out why v3.4.0 failed.\n\nNothing changed on payments-api; it's still on v5.1.0. I haven't re-checked error rates for either service since the rollback, so that's the next thing to look at.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PeQ4z927VFX15YR1FQN32b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GrV1hUZ8GKU8F1kcKiMDms", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0119boRpzq3jbHQ1aXiyFQ9L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tqv4JTzzw9s6a3M4SqZF1b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "too